{
  "id": "ss.relic.spurt",
  "name": "Growth spurt",
  "description": "The same pale grub twice: a small one low on the left and, laid over it and offset up-right, the same body at twice the size, same tilt, same segment bands, so the two read as before-and-after rather than as a pair. A short green sprout curls off the crown of the big one — the relic heals a quarter of the bar at every level-up, and a body that puts on size and then puts out new growth is the healing drawn as the growing. No eyes and no legs on either body: two ovals with faces would be two creatures, and legs at this size are arrows.",
